# Trimmed truth, transcriptions, exports and page renders for each row.
#
# All of it is regenerable: the truth from the reference .mxl plus the measure
# window in works.json, the prediction from the PDF plus the production weights.
# The root .gitignore already rules that benchmarks/**/*.omr.json is a dump
# rather than a record — "Commit the REPORT that cites the numbers, not the dump
# it read them from" — and the same holds for the rest of this directory. A
# single scanned orchestral page's .omr.json runs to six figures of lines.
#
# What IS committed lives outside fixtures/: works.json (hand-verified windows
# and staff maps, irreplaceable), the scripts, results.json (small), and the
# reports.
fixtures/

# Page renders made while establishing or re-verifying a measure count. Same
# principle as benchmarks/*/page-thumbnails/ and benchmarks/**/crops/ — seconds
# to regenerate from the PDF, heavy to carry.
pages/
*.png

# EXCEPT the committed verification-evidence crops for the 2026-09-05 drafted
# rows: 33 small clips (~2 MB total) of the printed measure numbers, margins
# and engraving facts ROW_VERIFICATION_CHECKLIST_2026-09-05.md asks Sean to
# confirm — the checklist links to them by filename, and the 09-04 tranche was
# verified entirely from such crops. Evidence behind a hand-verified window is
# a record, not a dump; the blanket *.png above stays for everything else.
!crops-2026-09-05/*.png
